  "reduction": "Each 1 nm vacuum cell's absorption line by line at each node (Voigt profiles, Humlicek 1982): every line of the stage's list over 360-780 nm by vacuum wavelength from a level below its ionisation limit, its strength in LTE per absorber of the stage (Boltzmann populations with Barklem and Collet 2016's partition functions, stimulated emission counted, no Saha factor: the column is the stage's own), its Doppler width thermal, its Lorentz width radiative (Kurucz's Gamma_rad, else the classical) plus van der Waals at the node's pressure of pure H2 (Barklem, Piskunov and O'Mara 2000's ABO width per H atom where their table holds the line, else Kurucz's own, each taken to H2 by Unsold's scaling, C6 proportional to the perturber's polarisability, else Unsold's per perturber, a neutral atom's from an upper level of n* 6 or more and at least 0.1 from an integer bounded by the high-Rydberg width 2 v N (sigma_pol + sigma_F), Alekseev and Sobel'man 1966 and Omont 1977, decision-r08-t4e-unsold); cut off 25 cm-1 from each line's centre at every pressure (Na D's and K's far wings beyond it are their pairs' cross-sections), nodes whose cell's intensity-weighted Lorentz half-width passes 0.25 cm-1 estimated; sorted into its k-distribution and reduced to two-point Gauss-Legendre g-intervals shared by every node of the cell, by bisection to 8e-4 in T over every column to 400 p_eff / (m g) at g = 0.5 m s-2 and helium's Rayleigh column; temperature nodes on the stage's ladder (E1, decision-r08-t4ef-storage section 5.3, or E1', decision-r08-t4e-budget section 3) from its visibility floor, refined by bisection to a quarter of E1's step where the chain test (cubic in T on ln sigma, the client's rows at the standard pressures each read between the table's nodes, the read cubic in ln p on tau) fails 2e-3; alternate pressure nodes below 1 MPa dropped where it passes (E3), and an 8-a-decade midpoint added between two held rows below 1 MPa where it fails by the read itself (decision-r08-t4e-unsold's follow-up); ln sigma stored in 16 bits a value (decision-r08-t4d-kdist.md; decision-r08-t4d-kdist-chain.md). The between-node test also stops at 400 p_sat / (m g) at g = 0.5 m s-2, p_sat NIST Chemistry WebBook's Antoine fit for liquid K after E. F. Fiock and W. H. Rodebush, J. Am. Chem. Soc. 48 (1926) 2522, 679.4-1033 K, used from 650 K (R08.T4.e's residual protocol, item (ii), decision-r08-t4e-unsold), errors beyond it recorded, not gated.",
